---
import ItemPage from '../../layouts/ItemPage.astro';
import { CAKE_SIZES } from '../../data/cakes';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much is a 10-inch Dairy Queen cake?', a: 'A classic 10-inch DQ cake typically costs about $32.99. Blizzard flavors in the 10-inch size cost about $35.99 to $38.74. Prices vary by location.' },
  { q: 'How many people does a 10-inch DQ cake feed?', a: 'About 12 to 16 people, depending on how big you cut the slices.' },
  { q: 'Can I get a custom message on a 10-inch DQ cake?', a: 'Yes. Most stores will write a name or short message for free. Custom designs and photo cakes usually need 24 to 48 hours’ notice.' },
  { q: 'Is the 10-inch cake better value than the 8-inch?', a: 'Usually, yes. It costs about $10 more than the 8-inch but serves 4 to 6 more people, so a slice works out to about $2.36 instead of $2.55.' },
  { q: 'How many calories are in a slice of a 10-inch DQ cake?', a: 'About 400. Dairy Queen lists the whole classic 10-inch cake at 5,570 calories, so 14 slices are roughly 400 calories each, or about 350 if you cut 16.' },
  { q: 'What Blizzard flavors come in a 10-inch cake?', a: 'Oreo, Cookie Dough, Choco Brownie Extreme and Reese’s Peanut Butter Cup are the usual 10-inch Blizzard cakes. Oreo typically costs about $38.74 and the others about $35.99. Freezer stock varies by store.' },
];
---
<ItemPage
  title="Dairy Queen 10-Inch Cake: Price & Servings (2026)"
  description="A 10-inch Dairy Queen cake costs about $32.99 and serves 12–16. Blizzard flavor prices, custom orders, lead time and how it compares to other sizes."
  name="Dairy Queen 10-Inch Round Cake"
  category={{ name: 'DQ Cakes', href: '/categories/dq-cakes' }}
  image="/Images/dq-cake-round-10inch.webp"
  imageAlt="Dairy Queen 10-inch round ice cream cake with decorated icing"
  badges={['Serves 12–16', 'Most popular party size']}
  quick="A 10-inch Dairy Queen cake costs about $32.99 for the classic chocolate-and-vanilla version and serves 12 to 16 people. Blizzard flavors in this size cost about $35.99 to $38.74. Order 24 to 48 hours ahead for a custom design. Prices vary by location."
  from="From $32.99"
  intro="The 10-inch round is the size most people pick for a birthday or office party. It has the same layers as every classic DQ cake: chocolate soft serve, a fudge and cookie crunch center, and vanilla soft serve under whipped icing."
  spec={[
    ['Price', '$32.99+ classic · $35.99–$38.74+ Blizzard'],
    ['Serves', '12–16 people'],
    ['Layers', 'Chocolate and vanilla soft serve, fudge and cookie crunch center, whipped icing'],
    ['Custom options', 'Message, colors; photo toppers at some stores'],
    ['Lead time', 'Same day from the freezer case; 24–48 hours for custom'],
  ]}
  allergens="Milk, Wheat, Soy"
  table={{ title: 'Compare DQ cake sizes and prices', ...CAKE_SIZES }}
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <h2>Is the 10-inch the right size?</h2>
  <p>For 12 to 16 guests, yes. If you have 10 or fewer, the <a href="/items/dq-cake-round-8inch">8-inch cake</a> is about $10 cheaper. For a classroom, team or big family party, a <a href="/items/dq-sheet-cake">sheet cake</a> feeds about 20 to 25 people and costs less per slice.</p>

  <h2>Classic or Blizzard flavor?</h2>
  <p>The classic cake is the safest choice for kids and mixed groups. A Blizzard cake blends a flavor like Oreo or cookie dough through the soft serve for a few dollars more. The <a href="/items/oreo-blizzard-cake">Oreo Blizzard Cake</a> is the most popular; the <a href="/items/cookie-dough-blizzard-cake">Cookie Dough Blizzard Cake</a> is a close second.</p>

  <h2>Every 10-inch DQ cake flavor</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table">
    <thead><tr><th>10-inch cake</th><th>Typical price</th><th>Per slice (14)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Classic (chocolate and vanilla)</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$32.99</td><td>$2.36</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="/items/cookie-dough-blizzard-cake">Cookie Dough Blizzard Cake</a></td><td class="price-cell">$35.99</td><td>$2.57</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Choco Brownie Extreme Blizzard Cake</td><td class="price-cell">$35.99</td><td>$2.57</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Reese’s Peanut Butter Cup Blizzard Cake</td><td class="price-cell">$35.99</td><td>$2.57</td></tr>
      <tr><td><a href="/items/oreo-blizzard-cake">Oreo Blizzard Cake</a></td><td class="price-cell">$38.74</td><td>$2.77</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Typical prices; your store may differ. The Reese’s cake contains peanuts.</p>

  <h2>Calories per slice</h2>
  <p>Dairy Queen lists the whole classic 10-inch cake at 5,570 calories. Cut into 14 slices, that is about 400 calories each; cut into 16, about 350. The full nutrition table is above.</p>

  <h2>How to order</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Check the freezer case for a ready-made 10-inch cake if you need one today. Staff can usually add a short message while you wait.</li>
    <li>For a custom design, Blizzard flavor or photo cake, order 24 to 48 hours ahead by phone, in store, or online where your store offers it.</li>
    <li>Keep it in the freezer until 10 to 15 minutes before serving.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Cutting and storage tips are in our <a href="/blog/dq-cakes-complete-guide">DQ cake serving guide</a>. Every size and flavor is on the <a href="/categories/dq-cakes">DQ cake prices page</a>.</p>
</ItemPage>
